   "source": [
    "* We're now going to use mSCA to infer latents and compare them to the ground-truth latents and corresponding time-delays.\n",
    "* **Note**:\n",
    "    * The recovered latents might appear a little bent when compared to the ground-truth. This is due to the non-linearities in the encoder. On real datasets (non-simulated), we've seen these non-linearities help find sparser, more interpretable latents.\n",
    "    * Also, the inferred latents may be flipped in sign (+1 or -1) when compared to the ground-truth."
   ]
  },
